  "notes": "McGill describes a three-storey, limestone Classical Revival building with the main gallery extending across the upper two levels and a semicircular rear. The surveyed published architectural analysis identifies the high banded basement, two recessed columns and two half-pilasters, main triangular pediment and tall glazed side elevations."
